M4.20 preflight gate execution-mode diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28

Error image
-----------
All 15 M4.20 unit tests raised `PermissionError` before the gate process could
start.

Cause
-----
The new gate file was created with mode 0644 while the tests invoke it through
its versioned shebang, consistent with the existing Control gates. The file
content compiled successfully and both JSON files parsed successfully. The
explicit Control `.gitignore` allowlist also did not yet include the new M4.20
machine artifacts and diagnoses.

Risk
----
Local validation had not executed and therefore could not support a completion
claim. No server command, GitHub write, service, database, token, provider or
runtime state was affected.

Rollback
--------
No server rollback is required. Repository rollback is branch abandonment or
revert of the M4.20 commit.

Approved correction
-------------------
Add only the exact M4.20 artifact paths to the Control allowlist, set the gate
to the same executable mode as existing gate scripts, and repeat the complete
M4.20 validation from the beginning.
